    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n53141" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κᾰπᾱνικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καπάνη</span>)
		dub. in <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ Θετταλικὰ</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεῖπνα</span>)<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> μὲν πολὺ καπᾱνικώτερα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					492
				</span></i>
			: expld. by <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				9.418d
			</span></i> as, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁμαξιαῖα</span>
			, <i>enormous</i>, by <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Χορταστικώτερα</span>,
				<i>more foodful, more plenteous</i> (from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καπάνη</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάπη</span>
			).</div>
